# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lesson gives an overview of programming models for distributing tasks optimally between resources."
msgstr "Pelajaran ini memberi gambaran keseluruhan tentang model pengaturcaraan untuk mengagihkan tugas secara optimum antara sumber."

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Programming models"
msgstr "Model pengaturcaraan"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore SPMD gres openmpi mpirun Gres SBATCH ntasks ntask cpus srun Sbatch sbatch squeue JOBID Pasqal optimiza OpenMP Iskandar Sitdikov */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore SPMD gres openmpi mpirun Gres SBATCH ntasks ntask cpus srun Sbatch sbatch squeue JOBID Pasqal optimiza OpenMP Iskandar Sitdikov */}\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Programming models are fundamental specifications that define how software is structured and executed. They provide a framework for developers to express algorithms and organize code, often abstracting away low-level details of the underlying hardware or execution environment. Different models are suited to different types of problems and hardware architectures, offering varying levels of abstraction and control.\n"
msgstr "Model pengaturcaraan adalah spesifikasi asas yang mentakrifkan cara perisian disusun dan dilaksanakan. Ia menyediakan kerangka untuk pembangun menyatakan algoritma dan mengatur kod, sering mengabstrakkan perincian peringkat rendah perkakasan asas atau persekitaran pelaksanaan. Model yang berbeza sesuai untuk jenis masalah dan seni bina perkakasan yang berbeza, menawarkan pelbagai tahap abstraksi dan kawalan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this lesson, we will review quantum and classical programming models and see how we can combine them to operate algorithms in heterogeneous environments. Iskandar Sitdikov gives us an overview in the following video.\n"
msgstr "Dalam pelajaran ini, kita akan mengkaji model pengaturcaraan kuantum dan klasik serta melihat bagaimana kita boleh menggabungkannya untuk mengendalikan algoritma dalam persekitaran heterogen. Iskandar Sitdikov memberi kita gambaran keseluruhan dalam video berikut.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<IBMVideo id=\"134680643\" title=\"In this video, Iskandar Sitdikov reviews quantum and classical programming models and examines how we can combine them to operate algorithms in heterogeneous environments.\"/>\n"
msgstr "<IBMVideo id=\"134680643\" title=\"Dalam video ini, Iskandar Sitdikov mengkaji model pengaturcaraan kuantum dan klasik serta mengkaji bagaimana kita boleh menggabungkannya untuk mengendalikan algoritma dalam persekitaran heterogen.\"/>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Programming model for QPUs {#programming-model-for-qpus}"
msgstr "Model pengaturcaraan untuk QPU {#programming-model-for-qpus}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will start with the programming model for quantum computers. The fundamental programming model which is familiar to nearly all quantum developers is the quantum circuit. We will not get into the details of the quantum circuit model here, as we already have a great [lecture by John Watrous](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/introduction) that explains this in detail. We will only mention that the circuit is built out of a set of lines (called wires) that represent qubits, gates that represent operations on quantum states, and a set of measurements.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan mulakan dengan model pengaturcaraan untuk komputer kuantum. Model pengaturcaraan asas yang dikenali oleh hampir semua pembangun kuantum ialah litar kuantum. Kita tidak akan masuk ke dalam perincian model litar kuantum di sini, kerana kita sudah mempunyai [kuliah yang bagus oleh John Watrous](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/quantum-circuits/introduction) yang menjelaskan ini secara terperinci. Kita hanya akan menyebut bahawa litar dibina daripada satu set garis (dipanggil wayar) yang mewakili qubit, get yang mewakili operasi pada keadaan kuantum, dan satu set pengukuran.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A quantum circuit diagram showing qubits as horizontal lines and quantum gates as boxes or connections between qubits.](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/programming-models/circuit.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A quantum circuit diagram showing qubits as horizontal lines and quantum gates as boxes or connections between qubits.](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/programming-models/circuit.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Another important programming model concept for quantum computing is what we call computational primitives. These primitives represent some of the most common tasks that users aim to accomplish with a quantum computer. There are several primitives available at the moment, including [Executor](/guides/directed-execution-model#executor-primitive). In this course we will focus primarily on the primitives Sampler and Estimator. Sampler gives you the ability to sample a state prepared by your quantum circuit. It tells you which computational basis states make up the quantum state prepared on your quantum circuit. Estimator allows you to estimate the expectation value of an observable for a system in the state prepared by your quantum circuit. A common context is estimating the energy of a system in a specific state.\n"
msgstr "Satu lagi konsep model pengaturcaraan penting untuk pengkomputeran kuantum ialah apa yang kita panggil primitif pengkomputeran. Primitif-primitif ini mewakili beberapa tugas paling biasa yang ingin dicapai pengguna dengan komputer kuantum. Terdapat beberapa primitif yang tersedia pada masa ini, termasuk [Executor](/guides/directed-execution-model#executor-primitive). Dalam kursus ini kita akan memberi tumpuan terutamanya kepada primitif Sampler dan Estimator. Sampler memberi Anda keupayaan untuk mensampling keadaan yang disediakan oleh litar kuantum Anda. Ia memberitahu Anda keadaan asas pengkomputeran mana yang membentuk keadaan kuantum yang disediakan pada litar kuantum Anda. Estimator membolehkan Anda menganggarkan nilai jangkaan bagi suatu boleh cerap untuk sistem dalam keadaan yang disediakan oleh litar kuantum Anda. Konteks yang biasa ialah menganggarkan tenaga sistem dalam keadaan tertentu.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A model histogram of results from sampler. Some states are very likely to be measured, others are very unlikely.](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/programming-models/sampler.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A model histogram of results from sampler. Some states are very likely to be measured, others are very unlikely.](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/programming-models/sampler.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last thing we are going to talk about in this section is transpilation. Transpilation is the process of rewriting a given input circuit to match the physical constraints and Instruction Set Architecture (ISA) of a specific quantum device. Similar to classical compilers, this means translating abstract unitary operations into the native gate set that the target device can execute. It also optimizes the circuit instructions for efficient execution on noisy quantum computers, with the routine gradually changing the circuit's structure by applying several optimization stages.\n"
msgstr "Perkara terakhir yang akan kita bincangkan dalam bahagian ini ialah transpilasi. Transpilasi adalah proses menulis semula litar input yang diberikan untuk memadankan kekangan fizikal dan Instruction Set Architecture (ISA) peranti kuantum tertentu. Serupa dengan pengkompil klasik, ini bermakna menterjemahkan operasi kesatuan abstrak kepada set get natif yang boleh dilaksanakan oleh peranti sasaran. Ia juga mengoptimumkan arahan litar untuk pelaksanaan yang cekap pada komputer kuantum berderau, dengan rutin yang secara beransur-ansur mengubah struktur litar dengan menggunakan beberapa peringkat pengoptimuman.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A diagram of transpilation showing how an abstract circuit is mapped into an instruction set architecture circuit. That is, the circuit is rewritten using the native gates and connectivity of the target hardware.](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/programming-models/transpilation.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Rajah transpilasi yang menunjukkan bagaimana litar abstrak dipetakan ke dalam litar seni bina set arahan. Iaitu, litar ditulis semula menggunakan get natif dan sambungan perkakasan sasaran.](/learning/images/courses/integrating-quantum-and-high-performance-computing/programming-models/transpilation.svg)\n"

